1
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:45,320
I don't know what you're planning,

2
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,720
but stop this. Leave it to the police

3
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:49,240
and trust the justice system.

4
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:52,200
Is Mungkorn betraying us?

5
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:54,840
I'm glad everyone decided to continue.

6
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:59,480
When the whole team shows up like this,
doesn't mean you can trust everyone, huh?

7
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:05,160
Louis's method is to temporarily store
the dirty money

8
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:09,440
at Wisut's waste facility
before laundering it into the system.

9
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,800
<i>That place is heavily secured.</i>

10
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,680
<i>Angpao and Risa</i>

11
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,920
<i>is breaking into the CCTV system</i>

12
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,240
<i>and accessing the factory database</i>

13
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:19,920
<i>before the money truck arrives.</i>

14
00:02:19,999 --> 00:02:21,120
You're new here?

15
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,960
Yes.

16
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:25,680
Mr. Louis didn't inform you?

17
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:28,400
The regular guys
both came down with COVID.

18
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:30,480
Let me see your IDs.

19
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:32,920
Let me see your IDs.

20
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,000
Let me check.

21
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,600
-Yes.
-Here.

22
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:47,200
SOMSAK LAKLAMSAN

23
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,840
Everything checks out. Don't worry.

24
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:51,040
-Go on in.
-Wait.

25
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,880
Bring me their IDs for verification.

26
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,160
Hand them over. Wait a minute.

27
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:01,720
Are you connected yet?

28
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:03,800
My fingers are flying. Why do you ask?

29
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,760
-Hurry up.
-Yeah, I know.

30
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,280
SOMSAK LAKLAMSAN, SANGA SONGSOMSUAN

31
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:21,280
FIRST NAME - LAST NAME

32
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,400
SANGA SONGSOMSUAN

33
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:31,960
Done. I hope we made it in time.

34
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,320
SANGA SONGSOMSUAN, VERIFY

35
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:50,400
SANGA SONGSOMSUAN

36
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,840
Hey, Koh.

37
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,800
You're good to go.

38
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:06,400
Thank you so much, sir.

39
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:09,040
Open the gate. Let them in.

40
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:11,400
-Let's go.
-Move it.

41
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,560
Hello, boss.

42
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:25,680
The money truck has successfully entered
the waste facility.

43
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,120
Alright.

44
00:04:27,199 --> 00:04:29,199
Then you can all head back.

45
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:01,000
Peanuts, sir?

46
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:03,040
Whoa, you scared me!

47
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:05,960
Sorry. I'm a police officer.

48
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:08,400
Could you buy some, sir?

49
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,400
Please?

50
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:13,720
Oh no, they're all crushed.

51
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:15,720
I'll take them.

52
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:22,680
-Just give me that much.
-This much, sir?

53
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:29,400
Thank you, sir.
You're such a kind police officer.

54
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,600
Thank you, sir.

55
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:54,000
PAPER RECYCLING FACILITY

56
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:23,080
Koh, stay out of the CCTV cameras.

57
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:25,400
I don't know if Angpao
has hacked the system yet.

58
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:36,480
-Open the back of the truck.
-Yes, sir.

59
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,080
Hey, start unloading.

60
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:48,360
I'm in.

61
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:51,600
The CCTV system
is fully under my control now.

62
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,840
Go ahead.

63
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:56,160
Move it.

64
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,520
Let me help you push.

65
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:02,480
We're in a bit of a hurry today.

66
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,920
Sure.

67
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:09,040
-Go.
-Sak.

68
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,120
Help me out here.

69
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,960
-Yes, bro.
-Yeah.

70
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:13,600
Let's get this done quickly.

71
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,120
Which way?

72
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,120
Wait here.

73
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:58,960
Ugh, I can't stop coughing.

74
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,160
Two, five, three.

75
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:15,480
Eight.

76
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:18,240
-Nine.
-Ris.

77
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,160
Can you believe it?

78
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:22,560
A tiny, cheap camera
is helping us move millions.

79
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:25,920
Stop talking. Is the CCTV feed clear yet?

80
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,480
I know. I'll take care of it.

81
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:37,440
What are you waiting for? Help load it up.

82
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,560
Done.

83
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:47,800
All set.

84
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:50,840
You're clear. Go ahead.

85
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:55,160
Nga, we're ready.

86
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,680
Hey, hurry up and load it.

87
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:00,960
Didn't you say you were in a rush?

88
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:01,880
Yes, sir.

89
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,320
Don't move!

90
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:23,000
Done.

91
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:26,040
This is too easy. After this job,

92
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:28,440
I'm taking Chen out for barbecue.

93
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:30,400
Now all we have to do
is move the money out

94
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,920
and leave without a trace,
just like we planned.

95
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,480
Hey, wait.

96
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,120
I see someone's car.

97
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,760
Whose car? Who's here?

98
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:46,040
I can't see clearly.

99
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:47,480
Hold on.

100
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:18,320
Mr. Louis, you came yourself?

101
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,680
The money truck has arrived, right?

102
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:22,000
It's been here for a while, sir.
They're unloading it.

103
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,080
Is something wrong?

104
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:24,720
I wanted to see it with my own eyes

105
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:26,600
that the money has arrived.

106
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:30,400
Louis is here.

107
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:36,360
He's entering the facility.

108
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:39,400
How did Louis get here, Koh?

109
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:41,320
Wasn't Mungkorn watching him?

110
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:43,960
Yeah. Why didn't he report this?

111
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:45,280
Koh.

112
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:46,760
If Louis sees our faces,

113
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:49,400
the whole plan is ruined.

114
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,120
I've got an idea.

115
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:54,960
Help me clear these guys.

116
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:56,480
-Koh, where are you going?
-I'll be back.

117
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:53,240
Hello, Mr. Louis.

118
00:12:58,320 --> 00:13:01,080
We've finished unloading the money.
We were just about to leave.

119
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:11,360
Why are you dressed like that?

120
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,080
There was a chemical leak.

121
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:15,640
We had to wear protective gear.
Otherwise, it could be dangerous.

122
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:17,160
You might want to wait outside.

123
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:20,240
Since when does this place
handle chemical waste?

124
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:33,600
Pesticides, sir.

125
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:35,520
They got mixed in with the plastic waste.

126
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,680
Someone sorted them incorrectly,
and they were burned together.

127
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:46,440
Where's the money?

128
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:49,160
It's already in the safe.

129
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:56,320
What's up?

130
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:58,960
My men reported that Wisut is fine.

131
00:13:59,040 --> 00:14:00,360
No movement yet.

132
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:02,600
Still, keep an eye on him.

133
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:06,440
-In case he tries anything.
-Got it.

134
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,120
Not so fast.

135
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,320
I want to see the money.

136
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:21,520
Open the safe.

137
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:27,560
Is there a problem?

138
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:31,200
-No, sir.
-Then open it.

139
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,880
<i>Two, five three.</i>

140
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:57,320
-<i>Eight, nine.</i>
-<i>Ris.</i>

141
00:14:58,400 --> 00:15:02,840
Can you believe it? A tiny, cheap camera
is helping us move millions.

142
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:11,440
Why isn't Koh entering the code?

143
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Maybe he can't remember.

144
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:35,560
What?

145
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:39,120
You entered it just a moment ago.
Don't tell me you've already forgotten it.

146
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:42,240
I entered it wrong.

147
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:44,320
Then try again.

148
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:49,120
Sorry, sir.

149
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:28,360
The last digit is two.

150
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:14,919
Report to the boss
that the money arrived intact.

151
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:15,960
Yes, Mr. Louis.

152
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:38,119
Okay. Louis is gone.
We're about to move the money out.

153
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,360
Copy that.

154
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,280
Where the hell is Mungkorn right now?

155
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:19,560
DEAD END, NO TURNAROUND

156
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:49,000
DEAD END, NO TURNAROUND

157
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:08,360
Hey, sir.

158
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,160
Is this your car?

159
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,200
Yes.

160
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:14,680
Is there a problem?

161
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:17,480
We received an order
to deliver food to your car.

162
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:20,920
Here you go, sir.

163
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:24,880
All set. Thank you.

164
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:51,360
That brat!

165
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:02,880
11 MISSED CALLS - RISA

166
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:21,160
Here he comes.

167
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:31,480
Is something wrong?

168
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:32,920
Where the hell have you been?

169
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:35,880
I had some issues.

170
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:42,960
Your job was to tail Louis
and keep us updated.

171
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:46,080
But you let him reach the facility.

172
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,800
You almost ruined everything.

173
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:49,520
I told you, I had a problem.

174
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:51,720
Sorry.

175
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:54,040
Is that all you've got to say?

176
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:56,280
Hey, sis. He already apologized.

177
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:58,200
What more do you want?

178
00:20:58,280 --> 00:20:59,880
We all run into problems, don't we?

179
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:02,320
This isn't the time
to blindly take someone's side.

180
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:05,320
Did your "problem"

181
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:07,720
have anything to do with you
talking to the police the other day?

182
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:14,000
Wait, sis. What are you talking about?

183
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:16,840
The day he went to meet with the police.

184
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:22,120
What are you thinking? Just say it.
Everyone almost died because of you.

185
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:24,120
Are you trying to betray the team?

186
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:26,040
Everyone, calm down.

187
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:29,480
I don't think Mungkorn would betray us.

188
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:30,400
Right?

189
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,560
If you think
I'm making baseless accusations,

190
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:36,440
I actually have proof.

191
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:37,520
Take a look.

192
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:38,800
Look.

193
00:21:57,240 --> 00:21:59,680
At first, I wanted you
to explain it yourself,

194
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:01,040
but you never did.

195
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:03,560
Are you a police informant?

196
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:05,400
Hey, this is going too far.

197
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:07,200
My friend would never do that.

198
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:12,840
That day, I was being followed
by the police.

199
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:16,680
I thought I could shake them on my own,

200
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:18,720
but I messed up.

201
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:22,680
They trailed me
when I went to monitor Louis,

202
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:25,560
so I had to lead them somewhere else.

203
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:28,920
Why would the police be following you?

204
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:31,920
I…

205
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:37,720
I don't know.

206
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:41,080
I'm not a kid. Just tell us the truth.
I don't believe you.

207
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:42,640
You're lying. Just look at yourself.

208
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:45,280
-Wait.
-I'm not a kid, damn it.

209
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:46,200
Wait.

210
00:22:48,840 --> 00:22:51,640
Our plan was to make them
lose trust in each other,

211
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:54,480
but now we're the ones
who don't trust each other.

212
00:22:55,080 --> 00:22:56,520
Isn't that ridiculous?

213
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:02,520
I've known Mungkorn for a long time.

214
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:04,400
He would never betray us.

215
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:10,800
If anyone still doubts Mungkorn,

216
00:23:12,480 --> 00:23:14,040
then you're doubting me too.

217
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:20,400
Okay?

218
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:35,520
Let's wrap up the money truck job.

219
00:24:08,520 --> 00:24:11,720
-Wow!
-Money!

220
00:24:13,360 --> 00:24:15,760
Money!

221
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:40,760
<i>We're receiving reports of a garbage truck</i>

222
00:24:40,840 --> 00:24:42,760
<i>crashing into a pharmacy.</i>

223
00:24:42,840 --> 00:24:45,720
<i>A large amount of cash</i>
<i>was found inside the truck.</i>

224
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:49,600
<i>Police have not yet determined</i>
<i>where the money came from.</i>

225
00:24:49,680 --> 00:24:51,560
<i>In addition,</i>

226
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:55,200
<i>police have discovered</i>
<i>that the pharmacy involved in the incident</i>

227
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:58,040
<i>is linked to an online gambling network.</i>

228
00:24:58,120 --> 00:25:02,200
<i>They are continuing their investigation</i>
<i>and expect to make more arrests.</i>

229
00:25:02,280 --> 00:25:06,240
I checked the money myself at the safe.

230
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:09,560
No one could've taken it.

231
00:25:12,040 --> 00:25:14,160
Unless Wisut is playing tricks.

232
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:18,640
He really got you this time.

233
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:31,920
All the money's gone?

234
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:33,760
Have you checked the CCTV footage?

235
00:25:33,840 --> 00:25:35,920
The CCTV footage
has been completely erased.

236
00:25:41,440 --> 00:25:43,200
What's going on?

237
00:25:44,280 --> 00:25:46,600
None of your business. Go upstairs.

238
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:52,760
Have you questioned all the guards?

239
00:25:52,840 --> 00:25:56,160
They said Mr. Louis arrived
some time after the money truck did.

240
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:02,960
We managed to recover footage
from a camera outside the safe.

241
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:14,320
Ris.

242
00:26:16,040 --> 00:26:18,400
If I leave this footage in the system,

243
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:21,320
won't Wisut suspect Louis even more?

244
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:26,440
With evidence like this,
they're bound to turn on each other.

245
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:32,680
Bring Louis to me. Now.

246
00:26:33,600 --> 00:26:34,760
Yes, sir.

247
00:26:50,040 --> 00:26:51,760
You need to keep a low profile for now.

248
00:26:51,840 --> 00:26:53,960
If things go south, I've already prepared
an escape route for you.

249
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:58,120
Make sure Thep doesn't say anything
that can be traced back to me.

250
00:26:58,200 --> 00:27:00,520
Don't worry. He won't say
a word about you.

251
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:06,840
Mr. Sorathep.

252
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:09,560
Stop lying to me.

253
00:27:10,600 --> 00:27:11,960
I already told you.

254
00:27:12,520 --> 00:27:15,360
I own this branch, understand?

255
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:17,080
I also own the online gambling site.

256
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:20,280
-If you don't believe me, check the lease.
-I don't believe you.

257
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:23,400
I know

258
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:26,720
<i>you're deliberately hiding something</i>
<i>to protect someone.</i>

259
00:27:33,640 --> 00:27:34,920
<i>Do you think the police are that stupid?</i>

260
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:39,040
Don't worry.

261
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:43,320
As long as your husband keeps quiet,
you won't die.

262
00:27:43,400 --> 00:27:45,080
You're just a nominee.

263
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:46,920
A front man.

264
00:27:48,680 --> 00:27:50,480
Tell me the truth.

265
00:27:54,680 --> 00:27:56,480
Stop lying.

266
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:01,200
Just tell me!

267
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:07,920
Let go!

268
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:10,480
Senior Sergeant!

269
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:12,760
If you're not going to arrest me,
then just kill me!

270
00:28:12,840 --> 00:28:15,280
<i>-Please!</i>
<i>-Put the gun away.</i>

271
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:17,000
Stay still.

272
00:28:22,880 --> 00:28:23,760
That's enough, Captain.

273
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,520
I'll handle this.

274
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:29,600
-Sir?
-It's alright.

275
00:28:29,680 --> 00:28:30,880
Go take a break.

276
00:28:31,600 --> 00:28:32,640
Yes, sir.

277
00:28:44,440 --> 00:28:45,640
Please, have a seat.

278
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:50,040
Go ahead.

279
00:28:52,720 --> 00:28:54,200
Sit down.

280
00:29:06,320 --> 00:29:07,880
Just tell me the truth.

281
00:29:10,680 --> 00:29:12,200
I promise.

282
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:16,120
Your wife and child will be safe.

283
00:29:30,280 --> 00:29:31,920
We're screwed.

284
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:34,960
Boss, the police are here!

285
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:36,440
Move!

286
00:29:36,520 --> 00:29:38,600
Stop! Drop your weapons!

287
00:29:40,480 --> 00:29:42,240
-Drop your weapons!
-Put them down!

288
00:29:44,200 --> 00:29:45,160
Stop!

289
00:29:48,320 --> 00:29:50,440
Code 24. Suspect fleeing
toward the end of the alley.

290
00:29:51,360 --> 00:29:54,760
Permission to report, sir.
The hostages have been rescued.

291
00:29:59,560 --> 00:30:01,160
Your wife and child are safe now.

292
00:30:01,920 --> 00:30:03,320
Really?

293
00:30:04,280 --> 00:30:05,120
They're safe?

294
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:07,440
Thank you.

295
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:11,920
-It's alright.
-Thank you.

296
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:20,040
Now, are you ready
to tell me the whole truth?

297
00:30:24,080 --> 00:30:25,000
Yes.

298
00:30:39,280 --> 00:30:41,200
Shit.

299
00:30:43,240 --> 00:30:44,800
Damn it. Let me go.

300
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,680
I've checked every channel.

301
00:30:59,760 --> 00:31:01,600
There's no news
that Louis has been arrested.

302
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:04,720
That guy could be hiding anywhere.

303
00:31:06,240 --> 00:31:11,040
Listen, kid, if both Wisut and the police
are after him, he won't get away.

304
00:31:12,080 --> 00:31:13,280
Yeah.

305
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:14,760
Let's just hope so.

306
00:31:15,480 --> 00:31:16,880
Otherwise, we're screwed.

307
00:31:16,960 --> 00:31:18,880
Where are Koh and Chen?

308
00:31:19,680 --> 00:31:21,120
Huh, Risa?

309
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:27,440
Why are you asking me? How would I know?

310
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:46,360
WHERE ARE YOU NOW? I NEED TO TALK TO YOU

311
00:31:46,440 --> 00:31:48,320
ABOUT LOUIS

312
00:31:50,120 --> 00:31:53,240
ARE YOU ALONE?

313
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:56,560
YES

314
00:32:00,120 --> 00:32:01,680
Hello. Where are you?

315
00:32:02,520 --> 00:32:04,680
Louis and his men are hiding at the pier.

316
00:32:11,480 --> 00:32:13,520
I'm looking for a chance to capture him.

317
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:16,240
Why didn't you tell me?

318
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:20,240
It's dangerous. I'm worried about you.

319
00:32:22,880 --> 00:32:24,160
Stop talking like that.

320
00:32:24,240 --> 00:32:25,400
Anyway,

321
00:32:26,240 --> 00:32:28,000
if I manage to catch Louis,

322
00:32:28,080 --> 00:32:30,440
I'll send you the location. Meet me there.

323
00:32:31,480 --> 00:32:32,680
And don't tell anyone.

324
00:32:33,400 --> 00:32:35,240
Wait.

325
00:32:55,800 --> 00:32:57,400
Who were you talking to?

326
00:32:59,840 --> 00:33:02,560
No one. I was just on my phone.

327
00:33:31,320 --> 00:33:32,240
Mr. Wisut.

328
00:33:32,320 --> 00:33:34,280
You dare betray me?

329
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:37,080
I swear, I don't know anything.

330
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:38,440
I really don't.

331
00:33:42,840 --> 00:33:44,280
Hey.

332
00:33:45,360 --> 00:33:47,560
-What are you doing? Stop!
-Lift your head.

333
00:33:58,280 --> 00:34:00,680
Do you have anything to tell me now?

334
00:34:01,400 --> 00:34:03,800
I swear, I really don't know anything.

335
00:34:04,600 --> 00:34:06,400
I have no idea
how the garbage truck incident happened.

336
00:34:07,120 --> 00:34:08,560
If you won't talk,

337
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:12,800
then die.

338
00:34:13,640 --> 00:34:15,880
Stop!

339
00:34:16,560 --> 00:34:18,880
Stop! I said stop!

340
00:34:27,120 --> 00:34:29,640
Louis! It was Louis.

341
00:34:29,720 --> 00:34:32,360
He planned everything. He set it all up.

342
00:34:33,120 --> 00:34:35,439
He was probably trying
to get revenge on you,

343
00:34:35,519 --> 00:34:37,240
but the accident ruined his plan.

344
00:34:38,600 --> 00:34:39,959
And where is he now?

345
00:34:40,039 --> 00:34:43,360
He's on the run, sir, but I know.

346
00:34:43,439 --> 00:34:45,039
I know where to find him.

347
00:34:48,959 --> 00:34:53,240
I heard they have a pier they use
as an escape route when things go wrong.

348
00:34:54,400 --> 00:34:56,479
A pier? Where?

349
00:34:57,400 --> 00:34:58,760
I don't know, sir.

350
00:35:05,840 --> 00:35:08,760
Coordinate with the local police.
Spread out and search every pier

351
00:35:08,840 --> 00:35:10,680
in Bangkok and the surrounding areas.

352
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:12,040
What about the Admin gang?

353
00:35:12,120 --> 00:35:14,400
Forget them for now.
Louis is about to escape.

354
00:35:14,480 --> 00:35:16,240
We have to catch him.

355
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:17,440
Yes, sir.

356
00:35:36,320 --> 00:35:38,040
Where have you been, James?

357
00:35:38,120 --> 00:35:39,960
<i>Big Tum figured us out.</i>

358
00:35:40,040 --> 00:35:41,840
<i>He sent his men after me</i>
<i>at Sorathep's wife's house.</i>

359
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:43,320
I barely made it out.

360
00:35:44,480 --> 00:35:47,480
I think they've already gotten
most of the information out of Thep.

361
00:35:47,560 --> 00:35:49,240
Otherwise, the police
wouldn't have issued warrants for us.

362
00:35:51,360 --> 00:35:53,760
We need to go into hiding.

363
00:35:55,760 --> 00:35:57,040
Where are you now?

364
00:35:59,200 --> 00:36:00,760
I'm at the pier.

365
00:36:01,480 --> 00:36:03,720
If you're coming with me, get here now.

366
00:36:05,240 --> 00:36:06,400
Got it.

367
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:24,000
There's one of Louis's men outside.

368
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:27,320
I don't know how many are inside.

369
00:36:28,040 --> 00:36:31,640
We should wait until it gets dark,
then move in and take him.

370
00:36:31,720 --> 00:36:33,480
Hey, seriously.

371
00:36:33,560 --> 00:36:36,400
Why didn't you tell everyone
what we were doing?

372
00:36:37,280 --> 00:36:38,320
Well…

373
00:36:39,960 --> 00:36:40,960
Yeah, why?

374
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:43,000
What's wrong with you?

375
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:45,040
Just kidding.

376
00:36:46,240 --> 00:36:48,400
I didn't want to put anyone else at risk.

377
00:36:49,440 --> 00:36:50,640
Then why bring me along?

378
00:36:51,440 --> 00:36:54,560
In case something goes wrong,
I can use you as a human shield.

379
00:36:54,640 --> 00:36:55,920
Thanks, my dear friend.

380
00:36:58,040 --> 00:36:59,680
Didn't want to put anyone at risk, huh?

381
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:02,120
Koh.

382
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:03,400
I can see right through you.

383
00:37:03,480 --> 00:37:04,920
What?

384
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:06,760
Come on.

385
00:37:06,840 --> 00:37:09,480
Ever since you came out
of the jungle with Risa,

386
00:37:09,560 --> 00:37:11,600
you've been getting pretty close to her.

387
00:37:11,680 --> 00:37:12,920
You were flirting with her earlier.

388
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:15,600
"It's dangerous. I'm worried about you."

389
00:37:18,600 --> 00:37:19,600
Say whatever you want.

390
00:37:19,680 --> 00:37:20,800
You like Risa, don't you?

391
00:37:21,800 --> 00:37:23,680
-Are you crazy? I don't.
-You do.

392
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:24,960
I don't.

393
00:37:25,040 --> 00:37:27,960
Then why are you blushing?
Look at you. Your ears are red too.

394
00:37:28,040 --> 00:37:30,120
-Louis is here. I'm serious.
-Don't change the subject, you idiot.

395
00:37:38,160 --> 00:37:40,320
-Where's James?
-We still haven't seen him.

396
00:37:41,760 --> 00:37:44,040
Refuel, and we're leaving.
No need to wait for him.

397
00:37:44,640 --> 00:37:46,040
Where the hell is he going?

398
00:37:46,680 --> 00:37:47,520
Yes, sir.

399
00:37:48,400 --> 00:37:50,360
There are only three of them.
I can handle it.

400
00:37:50,440 --> 00:37:51,680
Let's go!

401
00:37:51,760 --> 00:37:53,760
-Hey, wait.
-What?

402
00:37:59,640 --> 00:38:01,000
Is that James?

403
00:38:04,600 --> 00:38:05,880
Who is that?

404
00:38:09,320 --> 00:38:12,480
Hey, Louis. Mr. Wisut
sent us to send you off.

405
00:38:14,280 --> 00:38:15,480
Mr. Louis, run!

406
00:38:20,520 --> 00:38:21,840
After him!

407
00:38:26,720 --> 00:38:29,000
We're not the only ones
after Louis anymore.

408
00:38:29,800 --> 00:38:31,720
But we still have to get him.

409
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:44,920
Find him! Go!

410
00:39:22,600 --> 00:39:24,120
He's over here.

411
00:39:43,760 --> 00:39:44,960
Wait.

412
00:39:45,040 --> 00:39:47,600
You lure him downstairs.
I'll finish him off upstairs

413
00:39:47,680 --> 00:39:49,320
Go.

414
00:39:51,320 --> 00:39:52,600
You think you're getting
out of this alive?

415
00:39:52,680 --> 00:39:54,720
Go meet the Grim Reaper, you bastard!

416
00:41:08,560 --> 00:41:09,520
Chen!

417
00:41:15,760 --> 00:41:17,720
Koh, why are you helping Louis?

418
00:41:17,800 --> 00:41:19,600
I can't let him die yet.

419
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:22,480
-Come on.
-Move.

420
00:41:22,560 --> 00:41:25,720
Koh, wait. What the hell is going on?

421
00:41:39,520 --> 00:41:41,840
Wait, Louis. It's me.

422
00:41:41,920 --> 00:41:43,040
James.

423
00:41:43,120 --> 00:41:44,720
Where the hell have you been?

424
00:41:45,520 --> 00:41:46,560
Come on.

425
00:41:46,640 --> 00:41:48,800
I wasn't about to leave you behind.

426
00:41:48,880 --> 00:41:51,400
Enough talking. Let's move.

427
00:41:56,160 --> 00:41:57,600
MR. WISUT

428
00:42:02,560 --> 00:42:03,640
Why aren't you answering?

429
00:42:05,840 --> 00:42:07,480
Who's calling?

430
00:42:08,600 --> 00:42:10,400
Oh, it's my mom.

431
00:42:14,320 --> 00:42:15,440
Hold on.

432
00:42:16,320 --> 00:42:20,000
Hello, Mom. I'll call you back.
I'm busy right now.

433
00:42:20,080 --> 00:42:21,680
<i>Do you have Louis?</i>

434
00:42:25,640 --> 00:42:27,280
<i>Did you hear me?</i>

435
00:42:28,360 --> 00:42:30,480
MR. WISUT

436
00:42:31,480 --> 00:42:34,920
<i>Hello? Hello?</i>

437
00:42:49,920 --> 00:42:51,760
I knew it.

438
00:42:52,640 --> 00:42:54,720
I knew I couldn't trust you.

439
00:42:56,080 --> 00:42:58,360
Don't!

440
00:43:13,320 --> 00:43:14,400
Out of bullets, huh?

441
00:43:19,880 --> 00:43:23,120
Finally, we got him. My head's been
killing me through all of this.

442
00:43:29,160 --> 00:43:30,000
Isn't that guy--

443
00:43:33,440 --> 00:43:35,320
Hey, Koh, didn't you say

444
00:43:35,960 --> 00:43:38,320
this guy fell off a cliff and died?

445
00:43:38,400 --> 00:43:39,920
Yeah.

446
00:43:41,240 --> 00:43:42,840
Even hell wouldn't take him.

447
00:43:42,920 --> 00:43:44,880
Let's just hope he doesn't wake up again.

448
00:43:46,080 --> 00:43:47,520
Load him up. Let's go.

449
00:43:47,600 --> 00:43:50,200
Wow, getting bossy all of a sudden.

450
00:43:50,280 --> 00:43:52,400
-Hey, aren't you going to open the door?
-Open it.

451
00:43:52,480 --> 00:43:54,480
You open it. I'll drag him in.

452
00:44:10,200 --> 00:44:11,960
You guys are still alive?

453
00:44:16,600 --> 00:44:18,800
Sorry to disappoint you.

454
00:44:20,320 --> 00:44:22,520
So everything that happened…

455
00:44:22,600 --> 00:44:23,600
It was all you?

456
00:44:25,720 --> 00:44:27,000
That's right.

457
00:44:30,360 --> 00:44:33,000
Do you know who you're messing with?

458
00:44:33,080 --> 00:44:35,200
If I make it out of this alive, I will--

459
00:44:35,280 --> 00:44:36,200
"I'll kill every last one of you."

460
00:44:36,800 --> 00:44:38,480
Is that what you were going to say?

461
00:44:38,560 --> 00:44:40,440
Too bad.

462
00:44:40,520 --> 00:44:42,000
You won't get the chance.

463
00:44:42,520 --> 00:44:44,320
And you won't be saying another word.

464
00:44:44,400 --> 00:44:46,720
Shut your mouth.

465
00:44:49,520 --> 00:44:50,360
Don't say a word.

466
00:45:11,160 --> 00:45:12,280
How is it?

467
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:13,880
Hello.

468
00:45:13,960 --> 00:45:15,720
Four bodies were found
inside the warehouse.

469
00:45:15,800 --> 00:45:17,480
At the back of the warehouse,
another body was found.

470
00:45:17,560 --> 00:45:21,320
The documents in his wallet
confirm he's a police officer.

471
00:45:21,400 --> 00:45:22,320
A police officer?

472
00:45:22,400 --> 00:45:23,240
Yes, sir.

473
00:45:47,440 --> 00:45:51,440
Sir, the deceased officer was identified
as Pol. Lt. Col. Ruangrit Chokanun.

474
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:57,560
As for Louis, we're coordinating
with the marine police to track him.

475
00:46:00,360 --> 00:46:01,400
Cancel that order.

476
00:46:02,480 --> 00:46:04,880
A fully fueled speedboat
is docked at the pier.

477
00:46:05,480 --> 00:46:08,280
He probably hadn't escaped yet
when the shootout broke out.

478
00:46:09,720 --> 00:46:13,200
Judging by the bullets
and weapons they used,

479
00:46:14,240 --> 00:46:16,280
it's obvious these were professionals.

480
00:46:17,760 --> 00:46:20,440
Louis must have gotten in the way
of someone powerful,

481
00:46:21,240 --> 00:46:23,000
so they sent people to silence him.

482
00:46:23,880 --> 00:46:25,160
But he managed to escape.

483
00:46:26,960 --> 00:46:28,720
So this involves someone powerful?

484
00:46:30,360 --> 00:46:31,480
How do you know that, sir?

485
00:46:32,280 --> 00:46:35,200
Because of the deputy superintendent
you just reported dead.

486
00:47:15,080 --> 00:47:16,320
Mungkorn.

487
00:47:19,600 --> 00:47:21,080
How did you get here?

488
00:47:21,160 --> 00:47:22,640
What about you, Ris?

489
00:47:25,040 --> 00:47:26,360
What are you hiding from me?

490
00:47:32,800 --> 00:47:34,160
Ris.

491
00:47:35,200 --> 00:47:37,440
What exactly are you
and Koh planning to do?

492
00:47:39,080 --> 00:47:41,680
Please, just go home.

493
00:47:43,200 --> 00:47:45,280
You trust Koh more than you trust me now?

494
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:50,600
Mungkorn.

495
00:47:51,720 --> 00:47:53,600
I asked him for help

496
00:47:53,680 --> 00:47:55,520
because he knew my dad,

497
00:47:56,200 --> 00:47:58,560
and he promised to help me find him.

498
00:47:58,640 --> 00:47:59,760
That's all.

499
00:47:59,840 --> 00:48:02,400
Then why can't you tell me
what you're really planning?

500
00:48:03,520 --> 00:48:05,680
I don't want anyone else
risking their life because of me anymore.

501
00:48:05,760 --> 00:48:07,080
Then why is Koh allowed to?

502
00:48:08,960 --> 00:48:11,080
Do you see me as an outsider now?

503
00:48:31,960 --> 00:48:34,440
Hey, stop fooling around.

504
00:48:35,560 --> 00:48:36,640
Move.

505
00:48:48,560 --> 00:48:49,840
Did you get him?

506
00:48:49,920 --> 00:48:51,720
Yeah.

507
00:48:54,480 --> 00:48:56,480
What the hell?

508
00:49:02,160 --> 00:49:04,640
Mungkorn, how did you get here?

509
00:49:06,200 --> 00:49:07,480
Get him inside.

510
00:49:10,160 --> 00:49:11,560
Go.

511
00:49:22,800 --> 00:49:25,000
You didn't say he was coming with you.

512
00:49:25,080 --> 00:49:27,400
Your plan is to kidnap Louis like this?

513
00:49:31,320 --> 00:49:32,440
Ris.

514
00:49:33,320 --> 00:49:35,160
Do you even realize what you're doing?

515
00:49:35,240 --> 00:49:36,680
If we take Louis like this

516
00:49:37,280 --> 00:49:38,640
and he gets away,

517
00:49:38,720 --> 00:49:40,720
we're all in danger.

518
00:49:44,680 --> 00:49:45,880
Calm down.

519
00:49:47,040 --> 00:49:48,840
I came up with this plan.

520
00:49:48,920 --> 00:49:50,240
If anything goes wrong,

521
00:49:51,000 --> 00:49:52,720
-I'll take full responsibility.
-How?

522
00:49:53,480 --> 00:49:54,880
If someone dies,

523
00:49:54,960 --> 00:49:56,120
are you dying with them?

524
00:49:56,200 --> 00:49:57,880
-Mungkorn!
-That's enough.

525
00:49:57,960 --> 00:49:59,400
Both of you, stop it.

526
00:50:06,760 --> 00:50:09,600
What are you laughing at?

527
00:50:09,680 --> 00:50:11,000
What's so funny?

528
00:50:15,720 --> 00:50:18,240
You guys are idiots. Seriously.

529
00:50:20,120 --> 00:50:21,360
Shut your mouth.

530
00:50:22,960 --> 00:50:24,320
Let's get to the point.

531
00:50:25,840 --> 00:50:29,760
What do you want from me?

532
00:50:46,080 --> 00:50:47,320
You know this person, don't you?

533
00:50:55,120 --> 00:50:56,080
And what do I get

534
00:50:56,680 --> 00:50:58,200
if I tell you?

535
00:50:59,080 --> 00:51:00,440
You won't get hurt.

536
00:51:02,120 --> 00:51:03,840
Little girl,

537
00:51:03,920 --> 00:51:05,720
you think a threat like that

538
00:51:06,400 --> 00:51:08,400
scares me?

539
00:51:10,080 --> 00:51:11,640
Want to try me?

540
00:51:12,280 --> 00:51:13,480
Take this.

541
00:51:23,680 --> 00:51:26,640
Looks like you're close to Aek, huh?

542
00:51:31,160 --> 00:51:34,040
Are you his daughter?

543
00:51:44,480 --> 00:51:46,240
I was right, huh?

544
00:51:47,880 --> 00:51:50,840
Never thought he had a daughter.

545
00:51:51,520 --> 00:51:52,680
You turned out

546
00:51:53,360 --> 00:51:54,960
just as rotten as he is.

547
00:51:56,320 --> 00:51:59,280
Stop talking and tell me where he is.

548
00:52:00,760 --> 00:52:02,840
Don't!

549
00:52:02,920 --> 00:52:04,240
Don't move…

550
00:52:04,840 --> 00:52:06,840
or she's dead.

551
00:52:08,520 --> 00:52:10,120
Drop the gun.

552
00:52:13,480 --> 00:52:15,120
I said, drop the gun!

553
00:52:18,520 --> 00:52:19,920
Chen.

554
00:52:39,040 --> 00:52:40,400
Kick it over here.

555
00:52:42,160 --> 00:52:43,400
Hurry!

556
00:52:51,080 --> 00:52:54,040
Hey, don't do anything stupid.

557
00:52:54,760 --> 00:52:56,360
Don't you dare.

558
00:53:07,880 --> 00:53:09,000
Move.

559
00:53:09,080 --> 00:53:11,880
Or I'll blow her head off.

560
00:53:11,960 --> 00:53:13,360
Move!

561
00:53:58,720 --> 00:53:59,920
-Watch out!
-Ris!

562
00:54:34,120 --> 00:54:36,920
Risa, are you okay?

563
00:54:38,120 --> 00:54:40,600
Ris!

564
00:54:51,240 --> 00:54:54,360
Ris! Where are you going?

565
00:54:55,920 --> 00:54:58,000
Don't go after him. He's already gone.

566
00:54:59,280 --> 00:55:00,080
This is all because of you.

567
00:55:01,800 --> 00:55:05,440
If you hadn't interfered,
I would've found out where my dad is.

568
00:55:06,880 --> 00:55:09,520
Do you really believe that?

569
00:55:10,680 --> 00:55:11,560
Yeah, I do.

570
00:55:23,480 --> 00:55:24,680
Ris.

571
00:55:26,520 --> 00:55:28,840
You don't understand anything, do you?

572
00:55:31,120 --> 00:55:33,160
You really don't understand, do you?

573
00:55:43,200 --> 00:55:45,040
Mungkorn.

574
00:55:45,120 --> 00:55:48,480
Maybe you should calm down
so we can talk this through.

575
00:55:50,680 --> 00:55:52,320
Mungkorn!

576
00:56:00,160 --> 00:56:02,400
You've got about five hours

577
00:56:02,480 --> 00:56:05,080
<i>to break through the security system,</i>

578
00:56:06,840 --> 00:56:10,080
<i>then find the safe and get the money out.</i>

579
00:56:10,160 --> 00:56:11,560
Look at this.

580
00:56:11,640 --> 00:56:13,520
Ta-da!

581
00:56:13,600 --> 00:56:14,720
<i>Why is there so little?</i>

582
00:56:14,800 --> 00:56:17,440
Did Wisut see through us already?

583
00:56:17,520 --> 00:56:21,520
<i>Weren't you supposed to call the police</i>
<i>after we moved all the money out?</i>

584
00:56:21,600 --> 00:56:23,800
Everyone, we've been set up.
We need to get out of here now.

585
00:56:24,440 --> 00:56:26,480
How are we supposed to escape
with cops all over the place?

586
00:56:26,560 --> 00:56:29,320
-<i>How am I supposed to distract the police?</i>
-<i>Any way you can.</i>

587
00:56:29,400 --> 00:56:30,240
<i>Officer!</i>

588
00:56:31,840 --> 00:56:33,520
-Move.
-Hurry.

589
00:56:33,600 --> 00:56:35,160
Wait.

590
00:56:35,240 --> 00:56:36,400
<i>They're inside the house.</i>

591
00:57:24,120 --> 00:57:26,200
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
